From fd785f26428a5f44086ec4b8cd5334af7252194f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tangelo Dev <tangelo-dev@noreply.invalid>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 20:52:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] core/qt/android: the game report also lists the games in the game folders

The opt-in game report only listed installed titles, so games played from
the game folders (often a network folder with backups) showed up only once
started. Both game lists now hand their folders' title IDs to the report
when they have loaded (Qt: the game list's own folders; Android: the
games folder, through NativeLibrary.setGameFolderTitles), and every report
sends them as "folder". Until a game list has loaded, "folder" is left out
so the server keeps what it knew.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FYz3krf43qKGY6aS2Z5snz
